    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Hatshepsut began as regent for her young stepson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> and by Year 7 of his reign had taken the full royal titulary as senior coregent.</li><li>Her reign was a time of prosperity and general peace, marked by the expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-punt">Punt</a> and hundreds of building projects across Upper and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-egypt">Lower Egypt</a>.</li><li>Late in the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> and under Amenhotep II her statues were destroyed and her monuments defaced, so that she almost disappeared from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s records.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Unfinished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obelisk">Obelisk</a> left at its quarry in Aswan broke while being cut for Hatshepsut's 16th year as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a>, and it still shows how obelisks were quarried.</p></aside>
    </section>

